# Rules Index

Read this map first; load each rule body only when its trigger fires, before the affected action. Do not bulk-load the directory. `../AGENTS.md` supplies the always-on entry point, not an instruction to preload every rule.

| Rule | Trigger |
|---|---|
| `authority.md` | Before design/implementation: human stack approval; decision ownership, root compatibility opt-in, autonomy and material decisions |
| `evidence.md` | Verification/self-review, completion claims, side-effect tools, skepticism or pushback |
| `skill-use.md` | Skill discovery/selection and binding workflow commitments |
| `execution-safety.md` | Before the first shell command and throughout execution; sandbox routing, secrets, long-running processes |
| `git-safety.md` | Staging, committing, pushing, destructive Git operations |
| `code-quality.md` | Stack research, code design/implementation/review, actual capability reuse, library-free flags/score, tests and domain vocabulary |
| `document-formats.md` | Creating/saving/substantially revising/sharing human-facing documents or choosing report/spec formats |

**Layering:** instructions → triggered rules; skill discovery → `../skills/INDEX` → selected `SKILL.md` → requested references. Rules may point to skills; skills must never link back to or depend on rule files. Do not duplicate rule text into skills.

**Maintenance:** load `skill-author` before editing `.agents/` governance and check https://agentskills.io and https://agents.md. Check the skill index before loading skill bodies.
